    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "When 0.20 mol of hydrogen gas and 0.15 mol of iodine gas are heated at 723 K until equilibrium is established, the equilibrium mixture contains 0.26 mol of hydrogen iodide."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The equation for the reaction is as follows."
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "latex": "\\text{H}_2\\text{(g)} + \\text{I}_2\\text{(g)} \\rightleftharpoons 2\\text{HI(g)}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "What is the correct expression for the equilibrium constant $K_\\text{c}$?"
    }
  ],
  "layout": "list",
  "options": {
    "A": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\dfrac{2 \\times 0.26}{0.20 \\times 0.15}$"
      }
    ],
    "B": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\dfrac{(2 \\times 0.26)^2}{0.20 \\times 0.15}$"
      }
    ],
    "C": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\dfrac{(0.26)^2}{0.07 \\times 0.02}$"
      }
    ],
    "D": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\dfrac{(0.26)^2}{0.13 \\times 0.13}$"
      }
    ]
  }
